n):\n- Added `export const KNOWN_ITEM_TYPES = new Set(Object.keys(ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS))` to `claim-office.ts`, deriving the valid-types set from the single source of truth (the premium table) instead of a second hardcoded list.\n- Updated `cli.ts` to import `KNOWN_ITEM_TYPES` from `claim-office.ts` and removed its local duplicate declaration.\n\n**Mass Calculation**:\n- Before: `cli.ts` local set — 6 constants (string literals) + 1 binding = 7 mass, fully duplicated with the 6 keys already existing in `claim-office.ts`.\n- After: 1 invocation (`Object.keys`) + 1 invocation (`new Set`) + 1 binding = 5 mass, computed once, reused via import (0 additional mass at each usage site).\n- Net effect: removed a redundant hardcoded 6-item list; single representation of \"known item types\" now lives with the base premium data it's derived from.\n\n**Rule 4 (Fewest Elements)**: Rest of the codebase (helper extraction like `countBy`/`countByType`, `meetsEnchantmentThreshold`, `findInsuredItem`, `validateNoNegativeDamageAmounts`/`validateDamageCountsWithinPolicy`) is already minimal — each abstraction is used in exactly the place it clarifies intent (e.g., shared `countBy` avoids duplicating map-counting logic between base-premium and claim-validation code), no unused or over-engineered abstractions found.\n\n**Tests**: All 42 tests passing. `tsc --noEmit` clean. `eslint` clean."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":3393,"output":952,"cacheRead":20138,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":24483,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1784915456444,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-2495ca00-3d48-4abc-9da6-52046f37acee","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"}],"stderr":"","usage":{"input":77913,"output":6104,"cacheRead":148732,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":0,"contextTokens":24483,"turns":13},"model":"requesty/vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","stopReason":"stop"}]},"isError":fal