*:\n- **Naming**: `computeCap` — kept as-is; it precisely names its behavior.\n- **Type accuracy (Rule 2 – Reveals Intent)**: Widened `type Item = { type: string }` to `type Item = { type: string; cursed?: boolean }`. The test suite already constructs items with a `cursed` flag (and several upcoming `it.todo()` scenarios reference cursed items), but the `Item` type didn't reflect this, causing `tsc --noEmit` to fail with `TS2353` even though Vitest's esbuild-based test runner silently ignored the type error. This is a real latent defect: the type was lying about the shape of domain objects.\n- **Mass**: Unchanged (4 -> 4) — this is a type declaration fix, not a runtime logic change, so APP mass (which measures runtime elements) is unaffected as expected.\n\nBenefits:\n- The codebase now type-checks cleanly (`tsc --noEmit` passes), removing a hidden inconsistency that could break under stricter CI/build tooling.\n- The `Item` type now honestly documents that items may carry a `cursed` flag, making it clear to future readers/implementers that `computeCap`/`computeInsuranceSum` deliberately ignore it (per the spec), rather than being unaware of it.\n- No duplication or unnecessary elements were found elsewhere in the file — `computeBasePremium`, `countByType`, and `computeInsuranceSum` remain minimal and clear.\n\n**Step 7: Report Completion**\n\nRefactoring Complete:\n**Refactoring**: Widened the `Item` type to include the optional `cursed?: boolean` field, fixing a type-checking defect (`TS2353`) exposed by the latest test while keeping `computeCap`'s name and logic unchanged (it correctly ignores `cursed` per spec).\n**Mass Change**: 4 -> 4 (no change; fix was type-level, not runtime-logic)\n**Tests**: All 17 passing; `tsc --noEmit` now clean; `eslint` clean."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-30-56_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 17\nRecent Green phase: Added computeCap(items) returning computeInsuranceSum(items) * CAP_MULTIPLIER (2). The cursed flag on the item is present in the test but correctly ignored, since the cap is based on unmodified insurance value per the spec.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Use `NODE_ENV=development pnpm test` to run vitest tests.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 17\nRecent Green phase: Added computeCap(items) returning computeInsuranceSum(items) * CAP_MULTIPLIER (2). The cursed flag on the item is present in the test but correctly ignored, since the cap is based on unmodified insurance value per the spec.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Use `NODE_ENV=development pnpm test` to run vitest tests.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784912612136},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01JxReYrAmY8rfv3t4D6vAAP","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-30-56_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5/src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01N9MdNgZaEFLUEkNSwEkgw7","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-30-56_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5/src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":264,"output":243,"cacheRead":9756,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":10263,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784912612156,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-cea59403-0731-475b-a3f0-c2a15451d52c","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01JxReYrAmY8rfv3t4D6vAAP","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"export const roundUpToWholeG = (value: number): number => Math.ceil(value);\n\nexport const roundDownToWholeG = (value: number): number => Math.floor(value);\n\ntype ItemValueTable = Record<string, number>;\n\nconst ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS: ItemValueTable = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\ntype Item = { type: string };\n\nconst BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\nconst BLOCK_ELIGIBLE_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\n\nconst countByType = (items: Item[]): Map<string, number> => {\n  const counts = new Map<string, number>();\n  for (const item of items) {\n    counts.set(item.type, (counts.get(item.type) ?? 0) + 1);\n  }\n  return counts;\n};\n\nconst computePremiumForType = (type: string, count: number): number =>\n  BLOCK_ELIGIBLE_TYPES.has(type) && count === BLOCK_SIZE\n    ? BLOCK_PREMIUM\n    : count * ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[type];\n\nexport const computeBasePremium = (items: Item[]): number => {\n  let total = 0;\n  for (const [type, count] of countByType(items)) {\n    total += computePremiumForType(type, count);\n  }\n  return total;\n};\n\nconst ITEM_INSURANCE_VALUES: ItemValueTable = {\n  sword: 1000,\n  amulet: 600,\n  rune: 250,\n};\n\nexport const computeInsuranceSum = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + ITEM_INSURANCE_VALUES[item.type], 0);\n\nconst CAP_MULTIPLIER = 2;\n\nexport const computeCap = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  computeInsuranceSum(items) * CAP_MULTIPLIER;\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784912614570},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01N9MdNgZaEFLUEkNSwEkgw7","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport {\n  roundUpToWholeG,\n  roundDownToWholeG,\n  computeBasePremium,\n  computeInsuranceSum,\n  computeCap,\n} from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"MHPCO Claim Office\", () => {\n  // --- Rounding ---\n  it(\"rounds a premium of 197.5 G up to 198 G (favor of MHPCO)\", () => {\n    expect(roundUpToWholeG(197.5)).toBe(198);\n  });\n  it(\"rounds a payout of 350.5 G down to 350 G (favor of MHPCO)\", () => {\n    expect(roundDownToWholeG(350.5)).toBe(350);\n  });\n\n  // --- Base premium: main items & components ---\n  it(\"computes base premium 0 G for an empty item list\", () => {\n    expect(computeBasePremium([])).toBe(0);\n  });\n  it(\"computes base premium 100 G for a single sword\", () => {\n    expect(computeBasePremium([{ type: \"sword\" }])).toBe(100);\n  });\n  it(\"computes base premium 60 G for a single amulet\", () => {\n    expect(computeBasePremium([{ type: \"amulet\" }])).toBe(60);\n  });\n  it(\"computes base premium 80 G for a single staff\", () => {\n    expect(computeBasePremium([{ type: \"staff\" }])).toBe(80);\n  });\n  it(\"computes base premium 40 G for a single potion\", () => {\n    expect(computeBasePremium([{ type: \"potion\" }])).toBe(40);\n  });\n  it(\"computes base premium 50 G for 2 runes (no block)\", () => {\n    expect(computeBasePremium([{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }])).toBe(50);\n  });\n  it(\"computes base premium 60 G for 3 runes (block applies)\", () => {\n    expect(\n      computeBasePremium([{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }])\n    ).toBe(60);\n  });\n  it(\"computes base premium 100 G for 4 runes (no block -- requires exactly 3)\", () => {\n    expect(\n      computeBasePremium([\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n      ])\n    ).toBe(100);\n  });\n  it(\"computes base premium 175 G for 7 runes (no block)\", () => {\n    expect(\n      computeBasePremium([\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n      ])\n    ).toBe(175);\n  });\n  it(\"computes base premium 75 G for 2 runes + 1 moonstone (no block, different types)\", () => {\n    expect(\n      computeBasePremium([{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }])\n    ).toBe(75);\n  });\n  it(\"computes base premium 120 G for 3 runes + 3 moonstones (two separate blocks)\", () => {\n    expect(\n      computeBasePremium([\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"moonstone\" },\n        { type: \"moonstone\" },\n        { type: \"moonstone\" },\n      ])\n    ).toBe(120);\n  });\n\n  // --- Insurance sum & cap ---\n  it(\"computes insurance sum 1600 G for a sword and an amulet\", () => {\n    expect(\n      computeInsuranceSum([{ type: \"sword\" }, { type: \"amulet\" }])\n    ).toBe(1600);\n  });\n  it(\"computes insurance sum 2000 G for two swords\", () => {\n    expect(\n      computeInsuranceSum([{ type: \"sword\" }, { type: \"sword\" }])\n    ).toBe(2000);\n  });\n  it(\"computes insurance sum 1750 G for a sword and a block of 3 runes\", () => {\n    expect(\n      computeInsuranceSum([\n        { type: \"sword\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n      ])\n    ).toBe(1750);\n  });\n  it(\"computes cap 2000 G for a cursed sword based on unmodified insurance value 1000 G\", () => {\n    expect(computeCap([{ type: \"sword\", cursed: true }])).toBe(2000);\n  });\n\n  // --- Full quote premium pipeline ---\n  it.todo(\"computes premium 5 G for an empty item list (only the processing fee)\");\n  it.todo(\"computes premium 165 G for a newcomer's cursed sword (100 base + 50 curse + 10 first insurance + 5 fee)\");\n  it.todo(\"computes premium 95 G for a customer with exactly 2 years and a plain sword (loyalty discount applies)\");\n  it.todo(\"computes premium 145 G for a newcomer's sword with exactly enchantment 5 (high-enchantment surcharge applies)\");\n  it.todo(\"computes premium 115 G for a newcomer's sword with enchantment 4 (no high-enchantment surcharge)\");\n  it.todo(\"computes premium 195 G for a newcomer's cursed sword with enchantment 5 (both surcharges apply)\");\n  it.todo(\"computes premium 231 G for a cursed sword + plain amulet policy (curse surcharge scoped to the cursed item only)\");\n  it.todo(\"computes premium 160 G for a long-standing customer's second contract with a cursed, highly enchanted sword\");\n\n  // --- Claim processing ---\n  it.todo(\"pays out 400 G for a regular sword (enchantment 3), damage 500 G (full reimbursement minus deductible)\");\n  it.todo(\"pays out 100 G for a damaged rune (damage 200 G, no enchantment or material)\");\n  it.todo(\"pays out 400 G for a dragon-material sword, enchantment exactly 8, damage 1000 G (high-enchantment clause applies)\");\n  it.todo(\"pays out 400 G for a dragon-material sword, enchantment 9, damage 1000 G (both clauses apply; 50% rule wins)\");\n  it.todo(\"pays out 700 G for a dragon-material sword, enchantment 5, damage 800 G (only dragon-material clause applies)\");\n  it.todo(\"pays out 400 G for a steel sword, enchantment 9, damage 1000 G (only high-enchantment clause applies)\");\n  it.todo(\"pays out 600 G total when a dragon attack damages an insured sword (500 G) and amulet (300 G) (deductible applies per damaged item)\");\n  it.todo(\"pays out 800 G total when two insured swords are each damaged 500 G (each entry has its own deductible)\");\n  it.todo(\"pays out 1400 G with remaining cap 600 G for a first 1500 G claim on a sword (insurance sum 1000, cap 2000)\");\n  it.todo(\"pays out 600 G with remaining cap 0 G for a second 1500 G claim after remaining cap is 600 G\");\n  it.todo(\"rejects a claim where damages contain more entries of an item type than the policy insures\");\n  it.todo(\"rejects a claim where a damage entry's item is not part of t