n all tests so far: computes a surcharge that only applies when an item is *cursed* (50% of its base premium)\n- Question: Does \"computeItemSurcharge\" clearly reveal this intent, especially given upcoming todo tests reference enchantment surcharges too (\"high-enchantment surcharge applies\")?\n- Assessment: The name is too generic. The spec's test list already shows there will be *another* kind of item-level surcharge (enchantment-based) in upcoming tests. Keeping the generic name `computeItemSurcharge`/`itemSurcharges` risks collision/ambiguity once an enchantment surcharge is added — a reader wouldn't know which surcharge this function computes.\n- Recommendation: Rename to `computeCurseSurcharge` (and the local variable `itemSurcharges` → `curseSurcharges`) to precisely name what it currently — and will continue to — represent.\n\n**Decision**: Renamed `computeItemSurcharge` → `computeCurseSurcharge`, and `itemSurcharges` → `curseSurcharges`.\n\n**Current Code Mass** (before):\n```ts\nconst computeItemSurcharge = (item: Item): number => {\n  const base = ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type];\n  return item.cursed ? base * CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE : 0;\n};\n```\n- Constants: 1 (`0`) = 1\n- Bindings: 2 (`item`, `base`) = 2\n- Invocations: 1 (indexing `ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type]`) = 2\n- Conditionals: 1 (ternary) = 4\n- Loops: 0 = 0\n- Assignments: 0 = 0\n\nTotal Mass: 9 (unchanged by rename — pure renaming has no mass effect)\n\n**Refactored Code Mass** (after): identical structure, mass = 9. Mass Change: 9 → 9 (delta 0).\n\n**Rule Evaluation**:\n- Rule 1 (Tests Pass): ✅ All 19 tests remain green.\n- Rule 2 (Reveals Intent): ✅ Improved — name now unambiguously scopes the surcharge to curses, preempting confusion with the upcoming enchantment surcharge concept.\n- Rule 3 (No Duplication): No duplication found; skipped.\n- Rule 4 (Fewest Elements): Already minimal; no changes needed.\n\n**Refactoring Applied**:\n- Naming: `computeItemSurcharge` → `computeCurseSurcharge`; `itemSurcharges` → `curseSurcharges`\n- Mass: Unchanged (9 → 9) — this was a pure clarity improvement, not a structural one\n- Rationale: Rule 2 (clarity) took priority since APP mass was unaffected either way; the rename removes future ambiguity as the spec introduces enchantment-based surcharges\n\nRefactoring Complete:\n**Refactoring**: Renamed `computeItemSurcharge`/`itemSurcharges` to `computeCurseSurcharge`/`curseSurcharges` for clarity given upcoming enchantment-surcharge tests\n**Mass Change**: 9 → 9 (no change; naming-only refactor)\n**Tests**: All 19 passing"}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-30-56_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 19\nRecent Green phase: Implemented computeQuotePremium's full pipeline: policyBase = computeBasePremium(items); itemSurcharges = sum of computeItemSurcharge(item) for cursed items (50% of item's own ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type]); firstInsuranceSurcharge = policyBase * 0.1; total = policyBase + itemSurcharges + firstInsuranceSurcharge + PROCESSING_FEE; return roundUpToWholeG(total). The customer parameter is currently unused (prefixed with _).\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Use `NODE_ENV=development pnpm test` to run vitest tests.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 19\nRecent Green phase: Implemented computeQuotePremium's full pipeline: policyBase = computeBasePremium(items); itemSurcharges = sum of computeItemSurcharge(item) for cursed items (50% of item's own ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type]); firstInsuranceSurcharge = policyBase * 0.1; total = policyBase + itemSurcharges + firstInsuranceSurcharge + PROCESSING_FEE; return roundUpToWholeG(total). The customer parameter is currently unused (prefixed with _).\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Use `NODE_ENV=development pnpm test` to run vitest tests.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784913192316},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01GCwdtP4wz1qfvukUwG2FF4","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_012doyMMxWLNtqDuQSTJD6PC","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":368,"output":123,"cacheRead":9756,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":10247,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784913192335,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-9bac0189-b2d1-4816-ad91-a4da355b3641","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01GCwdtP4wz1qfvukUwG2FF4","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"export const roundUpToWholeG = (value: number): number => Math.ceil(value);\n\nexport const roundDownToWholeG = (value: number): number => Math.floor(value);\n\ntype ItemValueTable = Record<string, number>;\n\nconst ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS: ItemValueTable = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\ntype Item = { type: string; cursed?: boolean };\n\nconst BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\nconst BLOCK_ELIGIBLE_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\n\nconst countByType = (items: Item[]): Map<string, number> => {\n  const counts = new Map<string, number>();\n  for (const item of items) {\n    counts.set(item.type, (counts.get(item.type) ?? 0) + 1);\n  }\n  return counts;\n};\n\nconst computePremiumForType = (type: string, count: number): number =>\n  BLOCK_ELIGIBLE_TYPES.has(type) && count === BLOCK_SIZE\n    ? BLOCK_PREMIUM\n    : count * ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[type];\n\nexport const computeBasePremium = (items: Item[]): number => {\n  let total = 0;\n  for (const [type, count] of countByType(items)) {\n    total += computePremiumForType(type, count);\n  }\n  return total;\n};\n\nconst ITEM_INSURANCE_VALUES: ItemValueTable = {\n  sword: 1000,\n  amulet: 600,\n  rune: 250,\n};\n\nexport const computeInsuranceSum = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + ITEM_INSURANCE_VALUES[item.type], 0);\n\nconst CAP_MULTIPLIER = 2;\n\nexport const computeCap = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  computeInsuranceSum(items) * CAP_MULTIPLIER;\n\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\n\nconst computeItemSurcharge = (item: Item): number => {\n  const base = ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type];\n  return item.cursed ? base * CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE : 0;\n};\n\nexport const computeQuotePremium = (\n  items: Item[],\n  _customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number }\n): number => {\n  const policyBase = computeBasePremium(items);\n  const itemSurcharges = items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + computeItemSurcharge(item), 0);\n  const firstInsuranceSurcharge = policyBase * FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE;\n  const total = policyBase + itemSurcharges + firstInsuranceSurcharge + PROCESSING_FEE;\n  return roundUpToWholeG(total);\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784913194059},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_012doyMMxWLNtqDuQSTJD6PC","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport {\n  roundUpToWholeG,\n  roundDownToWholeG,\n  computeBasePremium,\n  computeInsuranceSum,\n  computeCap,\n  computeQuotePremium,\n} from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"MHPCO Claim Office\", () => {\n  // --- Rounding ---\n  it(\"rounds a premium of 197.5 G up to 198 G (favor of MHPCO)\", () => {\n    expect(roundUpToWholeG(197.5)).toBe(198);\n  });\n  it(\"rounds a payout of 350.5 G down to 350 G (favor of MHPCO)\", () => {\n    expect(roundDownToWholeG(350.5)).toBe(350);\n  });\n\n  // --- Base premium: main items & components ---\n  it(\"computes base premium 0 G for an empty item list\", () => {\n    expect(computeBasePremium([])).toBe(0);\n  });\n  it(\"computes base premium 100 G for a single sword\", () => {\n    expect(computeBasePremium([{ type: \"sword\" }])).toBe(100);\n  });\n  it(\"computes base premium 60 G for a single amulet\", () => {\n    expect(computeBasePremium([{ type: \"amulet\" }])).toBe(60);\n  });\n  it(\"computes base premium 80 G for a single staff\", () => {\n    expect(computeBasePremium([{ type: \"staff\" }])).toBe(80);\n  });\n  it(\"computes base premium 40 G for a single potion\", () => {\n    expect(computeBasePremium([{ type: \"potion\" }])).toBe(40);\n  });\n  it(\"computes base premium 50 G for 2 runes (no block)\", () => {\n    expect(computeBasePremium([{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }])).toBe(50);\n  });\n  it(\"computes base premium 60 G for 3 runes (block applies)\", () => {\n    expect(\n      computeBasePremium([{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }])\n    ).toBe(60);\n  });\n  it(\"computes base premium 100 G for 4 runes (no block -- requires exactly 3)\", () => {\n    expect(\n      computeBasePremium([\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n      ])\n    ).toBe(100);\n  });\n  it(\"computes base premium 175 G for 7 runes (no block)\", () => {\n    expect(\n      computeBasePremium([\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n      ])\n    ).toBe(175);\n  });\n  it(\"computes base premium 75 G for 2 runes + 1 moonstone (no block, different types)\", () => {\n    expect(\n      computeBasePremium([{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }])\n    ).toBe(75);\n  });\n  it(\"computes base premium 120 G for 3 runes + 3 moonstones (two separate blocks)\", () => {\n    expect(\n      computeBasePremium([\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"moonstone\" },\n        { type: \"moonstone\" },\n        { type: \"moonstone\" },\n      ])\n    ).toBe(120);\n  });\n\n  // --- Insurance sum & cap ---\n  it(\"computes insurance sum 1600 G for a sword and an amulet\", () => {\n    expect(\n      computeInsuranceSum([{ type: \"sword\" }, { type: \"amulet\" }])\n    ).toBe(1600);\n  });\n  it(\"computes insurance sum 2000 G for two swords\", () => {\n    expect(\n      computeInsuranceSum([{ type: \"sword\" }, { type: \"sword\" }])\n    ).toBe(2000);\n  });\n  it(\"computes insurance sum 1750 G for a sword and a block of 3 runes\", () => {\n    expect(\n      computeInsuranceSum([\n        { type: \"sword\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n      ])\n    ).toBe(1750);\n  });\n  it(\"computes cap 2000 G for a cursed sword based on unmodified insurance value 1000 G\", () => {\n    expect(computeCap([{ type: \"sword\", cursed: true }])).toBe(2000);\n  });\n\n  // --- Full quote premium pipeline ---\n  it(\"computes premium 5 G for an empty item list (only the processing fee)\", () => {\n    expect(computeQuotePremium([], { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 })).toBe(5);\n  });\n  it(\"computes premium 165 G for a newcomer's cursed sword (100 base + 50 curse + 10 first insurance + 5 fee)\", () => {\n    expect(\n      computeQuotePremium([{ type: \"sword\", cursed: true }], { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 })\n    ).toBe(165);\n  });\n  it.todo(\"computes premium 95 G for a customer with exactly 2 years and a plain sword (loyalty discount applies)\");\n  it.todo(\"computes premium 145 G for a newcomer's sword with exactly enchantment 5 (high-enchantment surcharge applies)\");\n  it.todo(\"computes premium 115 G for a newcomer's sword with enchantment 4 (no high-enchantment surcharge)\");\n  it.todo(\"computes premium 195 G for a newcomer's cursed sword with enchantment 5 (both surcharges apply)\");\n  it.todo(\"computes premium 231 G for a cursed sword + plain amulet policy (curse surcharge scoped to the cursed item only)\");\n  it.todo(\"computes premium 160 G for a long-standing customer's second contract with a cursed, highly enchanted sword\");\n\n  // --- Claim processing ---\n  it.todo(\"pays out 400 G for a regular sword (enchantment 3), damage 500 G (full reimbursement minus deductible)\");\n  it.todo(\"pays out 100 G for a damaged rune (damage 200 G, no enchantment or material)\");\n  it.todo(\"pays out 400 G for a dragon-material sword, enchantment exactly 8, damage 1000 G (high-enchantment clause applies)\");\n  it.todo(\"pays out 400 G for a dragon-material sword, enchantment 9, damage 1000 G (both clauses apply; 50% rule wins)\");\n  it.todo(\"pays out 700 G for a dragon-material sword, enchantment 5, damage 800 G (only dragon-material clause applies)\");\n  it.todo(\"pays out 400 G for a steel sword, enchantment 9, damage 1000 G (only high-enchantment clause applies)\");\n  it.todo(\"pays out 600 G total when a dragon attack damages an insured sword (500 G) and amulet (300 G) (deductible applies per damaged item)\");\n  it.todo(\"pays out 800 G total when two insured swords are each damaged 500 G (each entry has its own deductible)\");\n  it.todo(\"pays out 1400 G with remaining cap 600 G for a first 1500 G claim on a sword (insurance sum 1000, cap 2000)\");\n  it.todo(\"pays out 600 G with remaining cap 0 G for a second 1500 G claim after remaining cap is 600 G\");\n  it.todo(\"rejects a claim where damages contain more entries of an item type than the policy insures\");\n  it.todo(\"rejects a claim where a damage entry's item is not part of the policy\");\n  it.todo(\"rejects a claim with a damage entry amount of -200 G\");\n\n  // --- CLI integration ---\n  it.todo(\"CLI exits non-zero and writes an error to stderr for a quote with an unknown item type\");\n  it.todo(\"CLI exits non-zero and writes an error to stderr for a claim referencing an item not on the policy\");\n  it.todo(\"CLI exits non-zero and writes an error to stderr for a claim with a negative damage amount\");\n  it.todo(\"CLI processes a full scenario (quote then claim) and writes the results JSON matching the schema example\");\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784913194059},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01TWsEUXcrfkSeWHyVS32U2d","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-30-56_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5 && NODE_ENV=development pnpm test 2>&1 | tail -40"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":4343,"output":147,"cacheRead":9756,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":14246,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784913194059,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-d80b5ff8-3444-4f50-9334-6961f1bf5d28","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01TWsEUXcrfkSeWHyVS32U2d","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-30-56_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5\n> vitest run\n\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-30-56_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5\n\n ✓ src/claim-office.spec.ts  (42 tests | 23 skipped) 3ms\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  19 passed | 23 todo (42)\n   Start at  17:13:17\n   Duration  174ms (transform 31ms, setup 1ms, collect 29ms, tests 3ms, environment 0ms, prepare 53ms)\n\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784913197256},{"role":"