rge(item) + computeHighEnchantmentSurcharge(item);\n\nconst itemSurcharges = items.reduce(\n  (sum, item) => sum + computeItemSurcharge(item),\n  0\n);\n```\n- New function: Bindings 1 (`item`) = 1; Invocations 2 (`computeCurseSurcharge`, `computeHighEnchantmentSurcharge`) = 4 → 5\n- Reduce line: Constants 1, Bindings 3, Invocations 2 (`reduce`, `computeItemSurcharge`) = 4, Loop 1 = 5 → 13\n- Total: **18** (5 + 13)\n\n**Refactoring Applied**:\n- Rule 2 (Reveals Intent): Introduced `computeItemSurcharge` to name the concept \"total surcharge for one item,\" making the reduce body read as \"sum item surcharges\" rather than an ad-hoc arithmetic expression combining two surcharge sources.\n- Mass increased slightly (15 → 18) due to the extra function wrapper, but this is acceptable per the guideline that **Rule 2 (clarity) trumps APP** — the extraction makes the surcharge composition an explicit, named, independently testable unit that will scale cleanly if more surcharge types are added later (as the upcoming `it.todo` tests suggest).\n\n**Tests**: All 21 passing tests remain green; 21 `it.todo` tests unaffected.\n\n**Mass Change**: 15 → 18 (+3), justified by improved intent-revealing structure (Rule 2 priority over APP)."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":6244,"output":1021,"cacheRead":10072,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":17337,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1784913723307,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-7d96f9af-d709-4634-8f34-f4bef20cc34d","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"}],"stderr":"","usage":{"input":27184,"output":18637,"cacheRead":59800,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":0,"contextTokens":17337,"turns":6},"model":"requesty/vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","stopReason":"stop"}]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1784913733168},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01SpzBtd5gGXZEii3Fk8hon2","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-30-56_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5 && cat src/claim-office.ts && NODE_ENV=development pnpm test 2>&1 | tail -10"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":3459,"output":148,"cacheRead":150295,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":153902,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784913733172,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-b6356acc-8430-4fa7-a870-f1fbcde9ad89","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01SpzBtd5gGXZEii3Fk8hon2","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"export const roundUpToWholeG = (value: number): number => Math.ceil(value);\n\nexport const roundDownToWholeG = (value: number): number => Math.floor(value);\n\ntype ItemValueTable = Record<string, number>;\n\nconst ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS: ItemValueTable = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\ntype Item = { type: string; cursed?: boolean; enchantment?: number };\n\ntype Customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: number };\n\nconst BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\nconst BLOCK_ELIGIBLE_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\n\nconst countByType = (items: Item[]): Map<string, number> => {\n  const counts = new Map<string, number>();\n  for (const item of items) {\n    counts.set(item.type, (counts.get(item.type) ?? 0) + 1);\n  }\n  return counts;\n};\n\nconst computePremiumForType = (type: string, count: number): number =>\n  BLOCK_ELIGIBLE_TYPES.has(type) && count === BLOCK_SIZE\n    ? BLOCK_PREMIUM\n    : count * ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[type];\n\nexport const computeBasePremium = (items: Item[]): number => {\n  let total = 0;\n  for (const [type, count] of countByType(items)) {\n    total += computePremiumForType(type, count);\n  }\n  return total;\n};\n\nconst ITEM_INSURANCE_VALUES: ItemValueTable = {\n  sword: 1000,\n  amulet: 600,\n  rune: 250,\n};\n\nexport const computeInsuranceSum = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + ITEM_INSURANCE_VALUES[item.type], 0);\n\nconst CAP_MULTIPLIER = 2;\n\nexport const computeCap = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  computeInsuranceSum(items) * CAP_MULTIPLIER;\n\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.3;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\nconst LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.2;\nconst LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD = 2;\n\nconst computeCurseSurcharge = (item: Item): number => {\n  const base = ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type];\n  return item.cursed ? base * CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE : 0;\n};\n\nconst computeHighEnchantmentSurcharge = (item: Item): number => {\n  const base = ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type];\n  return (item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD\n    ? base * HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE\n    : 0;\n};\n\nconst computeItemSurcharge = (item: Item): number =>\n  computeCurseSurcharge(item) + computeHighEnchantmentSurcharge(item);\n\nexport const computeQuotePremium = (\n  items: Item[],\n  customer: Customer\n): number => {\n  const policyBase = computeBasePremium(items);\n  const itemSurcharges = items.reduce(\n    (sum, item) => sum + computeItemSurcharge(item),\n    0\n  );\n  const firstInsuranceSurcharge = policyBase * FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE;\n  const loyaltyDiscount =\n    customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD ? policyBase * LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE : 0;\n  const total =\n    policyBase + itemSurcharges + firstInsuranceSurcharge - loyaltyDiscount + PROCESSING_FEE;\n  return roundUpToWholeG(total);\n};\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-30-56_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5\n\n ✓ src/claim-office.spec.ts  (42 tests | 21 skipped) 4ms\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  21 passed 