pare 40ms)\n\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784913902975},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Green -- Implemented `processClaim` with per-damage deductible\n\nGreen Phase Complete:\n**Implementation**: `processClaim` sums `max(0, amount - 100)` per damage entry, rounding down\n**Result**: All tests now pass (26 passing, 16 todo)\n**Approach**: Minimal — no special clauses (dragon material, high enchantment) yet, since only the standard case has been tested."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01ChpeJfuVwCtX57e8qpdehy","name":"subagent","arguments":{"agent":"refactor","agentScope":"both","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 26\nRecent Green phase: Added processClaim(policyItems, incident) returning { payout } where payout = sum over incident.damages of max(0, damage.amount - DEDUCTIBLE(100)), rounded down via roundDownToWholeG. policyItems is currently unused (prefixed with underscore). No special reimbursement clauses (dragon material, high enchantment) implemented yet.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Use `NODE_ENV=development pnpm test` to run vitest tests.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":857,"output":459,"cacheRead":171071,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":172387,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784913902979,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-a96744fd-257c-4747-865b-6ea0d707c8e1","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01ChpeJfuVwCtX57e8qpdehy","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 26 tests still pass. Here's the refactoring report.\n\n**Naming Evaluation**:\n- Current name: `processClaim` — clearly reveals intent (\"process an insurance claim, return payout\"). Kept as-is.\n- Inline reducer used generic `damage` binding but repeated `Math.max(0, damage.amount - DEDUCTIBLE)` logic inline within `.reduce`, which is a per-damage-item calculation buried inside the aggregation logic. It didn't have its own name to describe \"reimbursement for a single damage entry after deductible\" — a concept that will need to grow (dragon-material clause, high-enchantment clause per the upcoming `it.todo`s). This *conceptual* naming gap was the improvement opportunity, not the outer function name.\n\n**Current Code Mass** (before):\n```ts\nexport const processClaim = (\n  _policyItems: Item[],\n  incident: { cause: string; damages: { itemType: string; amount: number }[] }\n): { payout: number } => {\n  const payout = incident.damages.reduce(\n    (sum, damage) => sum + Math.max(0, damage.amount - DEDUCTIBLE),\n    0\n  );\n  return { payout: roundDownToWholeG(payout) };\n};\n```\n- Bindings: 4 (`_policyItems`, `incident`, `sum`, `damage`) = 4\n- Constants: 1 (`0`) = 1\n- Invocations: 3 (`reduce`, `Math.max`, `roundDownToWholeG`) = 6\n- Loops: 1 (`reduce`) = 5\n- Assignments: 0\n- Conditionals: 0\n\nTotal Mass: 4 + 1 + 6 + 5 = **16**\n\n**Refactoring Applied**:\n- Rule 3 (No Duplication / conceptual clarity): Extracted the per-damage reimbursement calculation into a named helper `computeDamagePayout(damage)`. This isolates \"how much do we pay for one damaged item\" from \"how do we sum across all damages,\" which is exactly the seam the upcoming todo tests (dragon-material clause, high-enchantment clause, per-item cap) will need to extend without re-threading the reduce callback.\n- Added an explicit `Damage` type alias instead of an inline anonymous object type, reducing duplication between the parameter type and future reuse, and improving readability.\n- Renamed the reduce accumulator from `payout` to `totalPayout` to disambiguate it from the returned `payout` field.\n\n**Refactored Code Mass** (after):\n```ts\ntype Damage = { itemType: string; amount: number };\n\nconst computeDamagePayout = (damage: Damage): number =>\n  Math.max(0, damage.amount - DEDUCTIBLE);\n\nexport const processClaim = (\n  _policyItems: Item[],\n  incident: { cause: string; damages: Damage[] }\n): { payout: number } => {\n  const totalPayout = incident.damages.reduce(\n    (sum, damage) => sum + computeDamagePayout(damage),\n    0\n  );\n  return { payout: roundDownToWholeG(totalPayout) };\n};\n```\n- `computeDamagePayout`: Bindings 1 (`damage`), Constants 1 (`0`... actually `Math.max(0, ...)`) = 1, Invocations 1 (`Math.max`) = 2 → subtotal 4\n- `processClaim`: Bindings 4 (`_policyItems`, `incident`, `sum`, `damage`) = 4, Constants 1 (`0`) = 1, Invocations 3 (`reduce`, `computeDamagePayout`, `roundDownToWholeG`) = 6, Loops 1 = 5 → subtotal 16\n\nTotal Mass: 4 + 16 = **20**\n\n**Mass Change**: 16 → 20 (delta +4)\n\nMass increased slightly because we introduced a new named invocation and type. Per Rule 2 (Reveals Intent trumps APP), this is the correct trade-off: the upcoming test list (`it.todo`) already tells us `processClaim` must soon apply dragon-material and high-enchantment reimbursement clauses per damage entry — logic that belongs inside `computeDamagePayout`, not sprinkled across a reduce callback. Extracting it now keeps the design ready for that growth with minimal churn, and gives the \"per-damage reimbursement\" concept a name before it needs one.\n\nRefactoring Complete:\n**Refactoring**: Extracted `computeDamagePayout` helper and `Damage` type alias from `processClaim`'s reduce callback to isolate per-item reimbursement logic ahead of upcoming clause-based tests.\n**Mass Change**: 16 -> 20 (+4, justified by Rule 2 clarity/extensibility over raw mass)\n**Tests**: All 26 passing (16 todo unaffected)"}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-30-56_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 26\nRecent Green phase: Added processClaim(policyItems, incident) returning { payout } where payout = sum over incident.damages of max(0, damage.amount - DEDUCTIBLE(100)), rounded down via roundDownToWholeG. policyItems is currently unused (prefixed with underscore). No special reimbursement clauses (dragon material, high enchantment) implemented yet.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Use `NODE_ENV=development pnpm test` to run vitest tests.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 26\nRecent Green phase: Added processClaim(policyItems, incident) returning { payout } where payout = sum over incident.damages of max(0, damage.amount - DEDUCTIBLE(100)), rounded down via roundDownToWholeG. policyItems is currently unused (prefixed with underscore). No special reimbursement clauses (dragon material, high enchantment) implemented yet.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Use `NODE_ENV=development pnpm test` to run vitest tests.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784913908527},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_014bdTEs7Ww3CVmaR3fAi9VP","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01QFVvetsWkbUHsUrspC616X","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":303,"output":118,"cacheRead":9756,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":10177,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784913908547,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-47a2dde6-8d77-498a-aa21-37cebbb125cd","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_014bdTEs7Ww3CVmaR3fAi9VP","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"export const roundUpToWholeG = (value: number): number => Math.ceil(value);\n\nexport const roundDownToWholeG = (value: number): number => Math.floor(value);\n\ntype ItemValueTable = Record<string, number>;\n\nconst ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS: ItemValueTable = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\ntype Item = { type: string; cursed?: boolean; enchantment?: number };\n\ntype Customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: number };\n\nconst BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\nconst BLOCK_ELIGIBLE_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\n\nconst countByType = (items: Item[]): Map<string, number> => {\n  const counts = new Map<string, number>();\n  for (const item of items) {\n    counts.set(item.type, (counts.get(item.type) ?? 0) + 1);\n  }\n  return counts;\n};\n\nconst computePremiumForType = (type: string, count: number): number =>\n  BLOCK_ELIGIBLE_TYPES.has(type) && count === BLOCK_SIZE\n    ? BLOCK_PREMIUM\n    : count * ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[type];\n\nexport const computeBasePremium = (items: Item[]): number => {\n  let total = 0;\n  for (const [type, count] of countByType(items)) {\n    total += computePremiumForType(type, count);\n  }\n  return total;\n};\n\nconst ITEM_INSURANCE_VALUES: ItemValueTable = {\n  sword: 1000,\n  amulet: 600,\n  rune: 250,\n};\n\nexport const computeInsuranceSum = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + ITEM_INSURANCE_VALUES[item.type], 0);\n\nconst CAP_MULTIPLIER = 2;\n\nexport const computeCap = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  computeInsuranceSum(items) * CAP_MULTIPLIER;\n\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.3;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\nconst LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.2;\nconst LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD = 2;\n\nconst computeCurseSurcharge = (item: Item): number => {\n  const base = ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type];\n  return item.cursed ? base * CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE : 0;\n};\n\nconst computeHighEnchantmentSurcharge = (item: Item): number => {\n  const base = ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type];\n  return (item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD\n    ? base * HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE\n    : 0;\n};\n\nconst computeItemSurcharge = (item: Item): number =>\n  computeCurseSurcharge(item) + computeHighEnchantmentSurcharge(item);\n\nconst FOLLOW_UP_CONTRACT_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.15;\n\nexport const computeQuotePremium = (\n  items: Item[],\n  customer: Customer,\n  options: { isFollowUpContract?: boolean } = {}\n): number => {\n  const policyBase = computeBasePremium(items);\n  const itemSurcharges = items.reduce(\n    (sum, item) => sum + computeItemSurcharge(item),\n    0\n  );\n  const firstInsuranceSurcharge = policyBase * FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE;\n  const loyaltyDiscount =\n    customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD ? policyBase * LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE : 0;\n  const followUpDiscount = options.isFollowUpContract\n    ? policyBase * FOLLOW_UP_CONTRACT_DISCOUNT_RATE\n    : 0;\n  const discounts = loyaltyDiscount + followUpDiscount;\n  const total =\n    policyBase + itemSurcharges + firstInsuranceSurcharge - discounts + PROCESSING_FEE;\n  return roundUpToWholeG(total);\n};\n\nconst DEDUCTIBLE = 100;\n\nexport const processClaim = (\n  _policyItems: Item[],\n  incident: { cause: string; damages: { itemType: string; amount: number }[] }\n): { payout: number } => {\n  const payout = incident.damages.reduce(\n    (sum, damage) => sum + Math.max(0, damage.amount - DEDUCTIBLE),\n    0\n  );\n  return { payout: roundDownToWholeG(payout) };\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784913910628},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01QFVvetsWkbUHsUrspC616X","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport {\n  roundUpToWholeG,\n  roundDownToWholeG,\n  computeBasePremium,\n  computeInsuranceSum,\n  computeCap,\n  computeQuotePremium,\n  processClaim,\n} from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"MHPCO Claim Office\", () => {\n  // --- Rounding ---\n  it(\"rounds a premium of 197.5 G up to 198 G (favor of MHPCO)\", () => {\n    expect(roundUpToWholeG(197.5)).toBe(198);\n  });\n  it(\"rounds a payout of 350.5 G down to 350 G (favor of MHPCO)\", () => {\n    expect(roundDownToWholeG(350.5)).toBe(350);\n  });\n\n  // --- Base premium: main items & components ---\n  it(\"computes base premium 0 G for an empty item list\", () => {\n    expect(computeBasePremium([])).toBe(0);\n  });\n  it(\"computes base premium 100 G for a single sword\", () => {\n    expect(computeBasePremium([{ type: \"sword\" }])).toBe(100);\n  });\n  it(\"computes base premium 60 G for a single amulet\", () => {\n    expect(computeBasePremium([{ type: \"amulet\" }])).toBe(60);\n  });\n  it(\"computes base premium 80 G for a single staff\", () => {\n    expect(computeBasePremium([{ type: \"staff\" }])).toBe(80);\n  });\n  it(\"computes base premium 40 G for a single potion\", () => {\n    expect(computeBasePremium([{ type: \"potion\" }])).toBe(40);\n  });\n  it(\"computes base premium 50 G for 2 runes (no block)\", () => {\n    expect(computeBasePremium([{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }])).toBe(50);\n  });\n  it(\"computes base premium 60 G for 3 runes (block applies)\", () => {\n    expect(\n      computeBasePremium([{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }])\n    ).toBe(60);\n  });\n  it(\"computes base premium 100 G for 4 runes (no block -- requires exactly 3)\", () => {\n    expect(\n      computeBasePremium([\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n      ])\n    ).toBe(100);\n  });\n  it(\"computes base premium 175 G for 7 runes (no block)\", () => {\n    expect(\n      computeBasePremium([\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n      ])\n    ).toBe(175);\n  });\n  it(\"computes base premium 75 G for 2 runes + 1 moonstone (no block, different types)\", () => {\n    expect(\n      computeBasePremium([{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }])\n    ).toBe(75);\n  });\n  it(\"computes base premium 120 G for 3 runes + 3 moonstones (two separate blocks)\", () => {\n    expect(\n      computeBasePremium([\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"moonstone\" },\n        { type: \"moonstone\" },\n        { type: \"moonstone\" },\n      ])\n    ).toBe(120);\n  });\n\n  // --- Insurance sum & cap ---\n  it(\"computes insurance sum 1600 G for a sword and an amulet\", () => {\n    expect(\n      computeInsuranceSum([{ type: \"sword\" }, { type: \"amulet\" }])\n    ).toBe(1600);\n  });\n  it(\"computes insurance sum 2000 G for two swords\", () => {\n    expect(\n      computeInsuranceSum([{ type: \"sword\" }, { type: \"sword\" }])\n    ).toBe(2000);\n  });\n  it(\"computes insurance sum 1750 G for a sword and a block of 3 runes\", () => {\n    expect(\n      computeInsuranceSum([\n        { type: \"sword\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n      ])\n    ).toBe(1750);\n  });\n  it(\"computes cap 2000 G for a cursed sword based on unmodified insurance value 1000 G\", () => {\n    expect(computeCap([{ type: \"sword\", cursed: true }])).toBe(2000);\n  });\n\n  // --- Full quote premium pipeline ---\n  it(\"computes premium 5 G for an empty item list (only the processing fee)\", () => {\n    expect(computeQuotePremium([], { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 })).toBe(5);\n  });\n  it(\"computes premium 165 G for a newcomer's cursed sword (100 base + 50 curse + 10 first insurance + 5 fee)\", () => {\n    expect(\n      computeQuotePremium([{ type: \"sword\", cursed: true }], { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 })\n    ).toBe(165);\n  });\n  it(\"computes premium 95 G for a customer with exactly 2 years and a plain sword (loyalty discount applies)\", () => {\n    expect(\n      computeQuotePremium([{ type: \"sword\" }], { yearsWithMHPCO: 2 })\n    ).toBe(95);\n  });\n  it(\"computes premium 145 G for a newcomer's sword with exactly enchantment 5 (high-enchantment surcharge applies)\", () => {\n    expect(\n      computeQuotePremium([{ type: \"sword\", enchantment: 5 }], { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 })\n    ).toBe(145);\n  });\n  it(\"computes premium 115 G for a newcomer's sword with enchantment 4 (no high-enchantment surcharge)\", () => {\n    expect(\n      computeQuotePremium([{ type: \"sword\", enchantment: 4 }], { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 })\n    ).toBe(115);\n  });\n  it(\"computes premium 195 G for a newcomer's cursed sword with enchantment 5 (both surcharges apply)\", () => {\n    expect(\n      computeQuotePremium(\n        [{ type: \"sword\", cursed: true, enchantment: 5 }],\n        { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }\n      )\n    ).toBe(195);\n  });\n  it(\"computes premium 231 G for a cursed sword + plain amulet policy (curse surcharge scoped to the cursed item only)\", () => {\n    expect(\n      computeQuotePremium(\n        [{ type: \"sword\", cursed: true }, { type: \"amulet\" }],\n        { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }\n      )\n    ).toBe(231);\n  });\n  it(\"computes premium 160 G for a long-standing customer's second contract with a cursed, highly enchanted sword\", () => {\n    expect(\n      computeQuotePremium(\n        [{ type: \"sword\", cursed: true, enchantment: 7 }],\n        { yearsWithMHPCO: 3 },\n        { isFollowUpContract: true }\n      )\n    ).toBe(160);\n  });\n\n  // --- Claim processing ---\n  it(\"pays out 400 G for a regular sword (enchantment 3), damage 500 G (full reimbursement minus deductible)\", () => {\n    const policyItems = [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3 }];\n    const result = processClaim(policyItems, {\n      cause: \"fire\",\n      damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 500 }],\n    });\n    expect(result.payout).toBe(400);\n  });\n  it.todo(\"pays out 100 G for a damaged rune (damage 200 G, no enchantment or material)\");\n  it.todo(\"pays out 400 G for a dragon-material sword, enchantment exactly 8, damage 1000 G (high-enchantment clause applies)\");\n  it.todo(\"pays out 400 G for a dragon-material sword, enchantment 9, damage 1000 G (both clauses apply; 50% rule wins)\");\n  it.todo(\"pays out 700 G for a dragon-material sword, enchantment 5, damage 800 G (only dragon-material clause applies)\");\n  it.todo(\"pays out 400 G for a steel sword, enchantment 9, damage 1000 G (only high-enchantment clause applies)\");\n  it.todo(\"pays out 600 G total when a dragon attack damages an insured sword (500 G) and amulet (300 G) (deductible applies per damaged item)\");\n  it.todo(\"pays out 800 G total when two insured swords are each damaged 500 G (each entry has its own deductible)\");\n  it.todo(\"pays out 1400 G with remaining cap 600 G for a first 1500 G claim on a sword (insurance sum 1000, cap 2000)\");\n  it.todo(\"pays out 600 G with remaining cap 0 G for a second 1500 G claim after remaining cap is 600 G\");\n  it.todo(\"rejects a claim where damages contain more entries of an item type than the policy insures\");\n  it.todo(\"rejects a claim where a damage entry's item is not part of the policy\");\n  it.todo(\"rejects a claim with a damage entry amount of -200 G\");\n\n  // --- CLI integration ---\n  it.todo(\"CLI exits non-zero and writes an error to stderr for a quote with an unknown item type\");\n  it.todo(\"CLI exits non-zero and writes an error to stderr for a claim referencing an item not on the policy\");\n  it.todo(\"CLI exits non-zero and writes an error to stderr for a claim with a negative damage amount\");\n  it.todo(\"CLI processes a full scenario (quote t