ement to track cumulative claims against a policy (mentioned in the task), `processClaim` will soon need to combine this sum with prior-claims state — keeping the summation as its own named unit now makes that next change land as a small, local diff instead of restructuring an inline reduce.\n\n**Refactored Code Mass**:\n```ts\nconst sumDamagePayouts = (damages: Damage[], policyItems: Item[]): number =>\n  damages.reduce((sum, damage) => sum + computeDamagePayout(damage, policyItems), 0);\n\nexport const processClaim = (\n  policyItems: Item[],\n  incident: { cause: string; damages: Damage[] }\n): { payout: number; remainingCap: number } => {\n  const payout = roundDownToWholeG(sumDamagePayouts(incident.damages, policyItems));\n  const remainingCap = computeCap(policyItems) - payout;\n  return { payout, remainingCap };\n};\n```\n`sumDamagePayouts`: Constants 1, Bindings 4 (damages, policyItems, sum, damage), Invocations 2 (reduce, computeDamagePayout), Loops 1 (reduce×5) = 1+4+4+5 = 14\n`processClaim`: Bindings 4 (policyItems, incident, payout, remainingCap), Invocations 3 (sumDamagePayouts, roundDownToWholeG, computeCap → 6) = 4+6 = 10\n\nTotal Mass: 14 + 10 = **24**\n\nMass increased slightly (21 → 24) due to the extra function boundary (bindings for `damages`/`policyItems` params repeated), but Rule 2 (clarity/future-change locality) takes priority over raw APP mass here — this is an intentional, documented trade-off.\n\n---\n\nRefactoring Complete:\n**Refactoring**: Extracted `sumDamagePayouts` helper from `processClaim` to isolate the damage-summation concern ahead of upcoming multi-claim cap tracking (Rule 2/3 applied; naming confirmed unchanged as still accurate).\n**Mass Change**: 21 -> 24 (delta +3, accepted per Rule 2 > APP)\n**Tests**: All 34 passing, 8 todo unaffected."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":8170,"output":1471,"cacheRead":10031,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":196