aude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01JGnfsFQaMAxFWtLhdtyRD3","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import {\n  computeQuotePremium,\n  processClaim,\n} from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ntype QuoteStep = {\n  op: \"quote\";\n  items: { type: string; [key: string]: unknown }[];\n};\n\ntype ClaimStep = {\n  op: \"claim\";\n  policy: number;\n  incident: { cause: string; damages: { itemType: string; amount: number }[] };\n};\n\ntype Step = QuoteStep | ClaimStep;\n\ntype Scenario = {\n  customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number };\n  steps: Step[];\n};\n\nconst KNOWN_ITEM_TYPES = new Set([\n  \"sword\",\n  \"amulet\",\n  \"staff\",\n  \"potion\",\n  \"rune\",\n  \"moonstone\",\n]);\n\nconst validateItemTypes = (items: { type: string }[]): void => {\n  for (const item of items) {\n    if (!KNOWN_ITEM_TYPES.has(item.type)) {\n      throw new Error(`Unknown item type: \"${item.type}\"`);\n    }\n  }\n};\n\nconst readStdin = (): Promise<string> =>\n  new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\n    let data = \"\";\n    process.stdin.setEncoding(\"utf-8\");\n    process.stdin.on(\"data\", (chunk) => (data += chunk));\n    process.stdin.on(\"end\", () => resolve(data));\n    process.stdin.on(\"error\", reject);\n  });\n\ntype PolicyRecord = { items: { type: string }[]; remainingCap?: number };\n\nconst runQuoteStep = (\n  step: QuoteStep,\n  customer: Scenario[\"customer\"],\n  policies: PolicyRecord[]\n): { premium: number } => {\n  validateItemTypes(step.items);\n  const premium = computeQuotePremium(step.items, customer);\n  policies.push({ items: step.items });\n  return { premium };\n};\n\nconst runClaimStep = (step: ClaimStep, policies: PolicyRecord[]): unknown => {\n  const policy = policies[step.policy];\n  if (!policy) {\n    throw new Error(`Claim references unknown policy index ${step.policy}`);\n  }\n  const claimResult = processClaim(policy.items, step.incident, {\n    remainingCap: policy.remainingCap,\n  });\n  policy.remainingCap = claimResult.remainingCap;\n  return claimResult;\n};\n\nconst runScenario = (scenario: Scenario): unknown[] => {\n  const policies: PolicyRecord[] = [];\n  const results: unknown[] = [];\n\n  for (const step of scenario.steps) {\n    results.push(\n      step.op === \"quote\"\n        ? runQuoteStep(step, scenario.customer, policies)\n        : runClaimStep(step, policies)\n    );\n  }\n\n  return results;\n};\n\nconst main = async (): Promise<void> => {\n  const input = await readStdin();\n  const scenario = JSON.parse(input) as Scenario;\n  const results = runScenario(scenario);\n  process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify({ results }));\n};\n\nmain().catch((error: unknown) => {\n  const message = error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error);\n  process.stderr.write(`Error: ${message}\\n`);\n  process.exit(1);\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784915302559},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Refactoring Report\n\n**Naming Evaluation**:\n- Current name: `runScenario`\n- Function purpose: \"processes an array of steps (quote/claim), producing a results array\"\n- Assessment: Name clearly reveals intent already; no rename needed.\n- The inline branching logic inside its `for` loop, however, mixed two distinct responsibilities (quote handling vs. claim handling) in one block — that's the part worth improving, not the name.\n\n**Current Code Mass** (`runScenario`, before):\n```\nfor (const step of scenario.steps) {\n  if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n    validateItemTypes(step.items);                    // invocation\n    const premium = computeQuotePremium(...);          // assignment + invocation\n    policies.push({ items: step.items });              // invocation\n    results.push({ premium });                         // invocation\n  } else {\n    const policy = policies[step.policy];              // assignment\n    if (!policy) { throw ... }                         // conditional\n    const claimResult = processClaim(...);             // assignment + invocation\n    policy.remainingCap = claimResult.remainingCap;     // assignment\n    results.push(claimResult);                          // invocation\n  }\n}\n```\n- Loops: 1 = 5\n- Conditionals: 2 (`if quote/else`, `if !policy`) = 8\n- Invocations: 6 (validate, computeQuotePremium, push, push, processClaim, push) = 12\n- Assignments: 4 (premium, policy, claimResult, remainingCap mutation) = 24\n- Bindings: 3 (step, premium, policy/claimResult) ≈ 4 = 4\n\n**Total Mass ≈ 53**\n\n## Refactoring Applied (Rule 3: No Duplication / Rule 4: Fewest Elements)\n\nExtracted the two branches of the `quote`/`claim` conditional into `runQuoteStep` and `runClaimStep`, each named after the specific operation it performs. `runScenario`'s loop body is now a single ternary dispatch that pushes whichever step result was computed — the branching structure and per-step responsibility are now explicit at the call site instead of buried inside one large loop body.\n\n**Refactored Code Mass**:\n```\nrunQuoteStep:  invocations 3 (validateItemTypes, computeQuotePremium, push) = 6\n               assignments 1 (premium) = 6, bindings 2 = 2       → 14\nrunClaimStep:  conditional 1 = 4, invocations 2 (processClaim, push) = 4\n               assignments 2 (claimResult, remainingCap mutation) = 12, bindings 2 = 2 → 22\nrunScenario:   loop 1 = 5, invocations 3 (push + 2 dispatch calls) = 6, bindings 1 = 1 → 12\n```\n**Total Mass ≈ 48** (delta ≈ -5; more importantly, the loop body's cyclomatic complexity dropped from 2 nested conditionals to a single ternary, and each extracted function is independently testable/nameable.)\n\n**Benefits**:\n- `runScenario` now reads as \"for each step, dispatch to quote or claim handling and collect the result\" — the orchestration is separated from the per-op logic.\n- `runQuoteStep`/`runClaimStep` names make each operation's responsibility explicit, aiding future maintenance if quote/claim logic diverges further.\n- Slight mass reduction, but the main